{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "JOB",
  "chapter": 8,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "JOB.8.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.8.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then answered Bildad the Shuhite, and said,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.8.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.8.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "How long wilt thou speak these ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "things",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": "? and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "how long shall",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the words of thy mouth ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "be like",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a strong wind?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.8.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.8.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Doth God pervert judgment; or doth the Almighty pervert justice?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.8.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.8.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If thy children have sinned against him, and he hath cast them away for their transgression;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.8.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.8.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If thou wouldst seek to God betimes, and make thy supplication to the Almighty;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.8.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.8.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If thou ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "wert",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " pure and upright; surely now he would awake for thee, and make the habitation of thy righteousness prosperous.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.8.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.8.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Though thy beginning was small, yet thy latter end would greatly increase.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.8.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.8.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For inquire, I pray thee, of the former age, and prepare thyself to the search of their fathers:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.8.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.8.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "(For we ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are but of",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " yesterday, and know nothing, because our days upon earth ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a shadow:)",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.8.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.8.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Will they not teach thee, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " tell thee, and utter words out of their heart?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.8.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.8.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Can the rush grow without mire? can the flag grow without water?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.8.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.8.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Whilst it ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " yet in its greenness, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " not cut down, it withereth before any ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "other",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " herb.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.8.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.8.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "So ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the paths of all that forget God; and the hypocrite's hope shall perish:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.8.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.8.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Whose hope shall be cut off, and whose trust ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "shall be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a spider's web.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.8.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.8.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He shall lean upon his house, but it shall not stand: he shall hold it fast, but it shall not endure.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.8.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.8.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " green before the sun, and his branch shooteth forth in his garden.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.8.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.8.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "His roots are wrapped about the heap, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " seeth the place of stones.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.8.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.8.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If he shall destroy him from his place, then ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " shall deny him, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "saying",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", I have not seen thee.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.8.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.8.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Behold, this ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the joy of his way, and out of the earth shall others grow.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.8.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.8.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Behold, God will not cast away a perfect ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "man",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", neither will he help the evil doers:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.8.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.8.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Till he shall fill thy mouth with laughing, and thy lips with rejoicing.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.8.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.8.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They that hate thee shall be clothed with shame; and the dwelling place of the wicked shall come to naught.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
